{"path":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/index.html","title":"Workload API","description":"The Workload API resource defines the scheduling requirements and structure of a multi-Pod application. While workload controllers such as Job manage the application's runtime state, the Workload…","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workload API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"FEATURE STATE: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Kubernetes v1.35 [alpha]"},{"type":"text","value":"(disabled by default)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Workload"},{"type":"text","value":" API resource defines the scheduling requirements and structure of a multi-Pod application. While workload controllers such as "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/job/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Job"}]},{"type":"text","value":" manage the application's runtime state, the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Workload"},{"type":"text","value":" specifies how groups of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pods"},{"type":"text","value":" should be scheduled. The Job controller is the only built-in controller that creates "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/podgroup-api/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" objects from the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Workload"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroupTemplates"},{"type":"text","value":" at runtime."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"what-is-a-workload","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What is a Workload?"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/index.html#what-is-a-workload","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Workload API resource is part of the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"scheduling.k8s.io/v1alpha2"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/kubernetes-api/#api-groups-and-versioning","title":"A set of related paths in the Kubernetes API.","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API group"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and your cluster must have that API group enabled, as well as the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"GenericWorkload"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/command-line-tools-reference/feature-gates/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"feature gate"}]},{"type":"text","value":", before you can use this API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Workload"},{"type":"text","value":" is a static, long-lived policy template. It defines what scheduling policies should be applied to groups of Pods, but does not track runtime state itself. Runtime scheduling state is maintained by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/podgroup-api/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" objects, which controllers create from the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Workload"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroupTemplates"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"api-structure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API structure"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/index.html#api-structure","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Workload"},{"type":"text","value":" consists of two fields: a list of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroupTemplates"},{"type":"text","value":" and an optional controller reference. The entire "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Workload"},{"type":"text","value":" spec is immutable after creation: you cannot modify existing templates, add new templates, or remove templates from "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"podGroupTemplates"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"podgrouptemplates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroupTemplates"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/index.html#podgrouptemplates","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"spec.podGroupTemplates"},{"type":"text","value":" list defines the distinct components of your workload. For example, a machine learning job might have a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"driver"},{"type":"text","value":" template and a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"worker"},{"type":"text","value":" template."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each entry in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"podGroupTemplates"},{"type":"text","value":" must have:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A unique "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" that will be used to reference the template in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroup"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"spec.podGroupTemplateRef"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"scheduling policy"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"basic"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"gang"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/command-line-tools-reference/feature-gates/#WorkloadAwarePreemption","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"WorkloadAwarePreemption"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/command-line-tools-reference/feature-gates/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"feature gate"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is enabled each entry in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"podGroups"},{"type":"text","value":" can also have "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/disruption-and-priority/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"priority and disruption mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The maximum number of PodGroupTemplates in a single Workload is 8."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"yaml","code":"apiVersion: scheduling.k8s.io/v1alpha2\nkind: Workload\nmetadata:\n  name: training-job-workload\n  namespace: some-ns\nspec:\n  controllerRef:\n    apiGroup: batch\n    kind: Job\n    name: training-job\n  podGroupTemplates:\n  - name: workers\n    schedulingPolicy:\n      gang:\n        # The gang is schedulable only if 4 pods can run at once\n        minCount: 4\n    priorityClassName: high-priority # Only applicable with WorkloadAwarePreemption feature gate\n    disruptionMode: PodGroup # Only applicable with WorkloadAwarePreemption feature gate"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a workload controller creates a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" from one of these templates, it copies the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"schedulingPolicy"},{"type":"text","value":" into the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroup"},{"type":"text","value":"'s own spec. Changes to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Workload"},{"type":"text","value":" only affect newly created "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroups"},{"type":"text","value":", not existing ones."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"referencing-a-workload-controlling-object","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Referencing a workload controlling object"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/index.html#referencing-a-workload-controlling-object","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"controllerRef"},{"type":"text","value":" field links the Workload back to the specific high-level object defining the application, such as a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/job/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Job"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or a custom CRD. This is useful for observability and tooling. This data is not used to schedule or manage the Workload."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"gang-scheduling-with-jobs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gang scheduling with Jobs"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/index.html#gang-scheduling-with-jobs","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"text","value":"FEATURE STATE: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Kubernetes v1.36 [alpha]"},{"type":"text","value":"(disabled by default)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/command-line-tools-reference/feature-gates/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"WorkloadWithJob"}]},{"type":"text","value":" feature gate is enabled, the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/job/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Job"}]},{"type":"text","value":" controller automatically creates Workload and PodGroup objects for parallel indexed Jobs where "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".spec.parallelism"},{"type":"text","value":" equals "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".spec.completions"},{"type":"text","value":". The gang policy's "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"minCount"},{"type":"text","value":" is set to the Job's parallelism, so all Pods must be schedulable together before any of them are bound to nodes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the built-in path for using gang scheduling with Jobs. You do not need to create Workload or PodGroup objects yourself as the Job controller handles it automatically. Other workload controllers (such as JobSet) may manage their own Workload and PodGroup objects independently."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"what-s-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What's next"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/index.html#what-s-next","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learn about "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup scheduling policies"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"See how PodGroups are created from Workloads in the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/podgroup-api/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup API"}]},{"type":"text","value":" overview."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read about how Pods reference their PodGroup via the "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/pods/scheduling-group/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"scheduling group"}]},{"type":"text","value":" field."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learn about "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/topology-aware-scheduling/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Topology-aware workload scheduling"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Understand the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/gang-scheduling/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"gang scheduling"}]},{"type":"text","value":" algorithm."}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/disruption-and-priority/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pod Group Disruption and Priority"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup Scheduling Policies"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/topology-aware-scheduling/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Topology-Aware Workload Scheduling"}]}]}]}]}}
